For the basic graph $y=x^{n}$, an **even** power gives a **turning point** at the origin, with both arms rising and line symmetry about the $y$-axis.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-3.2,0)--(3.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-3.2)--(0,3.2) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-1.33:1.33,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{\x*\x*\x*\x});
\fill (0,0) circle (2pt);
\node[right,font=\small] at (0.3,-0.8) {turning point};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

For the basic graph $y=x^{n}$, an **odd** power gives a point of inflection at the origin, where the concavity changes, with the arms going opposite ways and point symmetry about the origin.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-3.2,0)--(3.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-3.2)--(0,3.2) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-1.25:1.25,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{\x*\x*\x*\x*\x});
\fill (0,0) circle (2pt);
\node[right,font=\small] at (0.35,-0.9) {point of inflection};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
Shift $y=x^{3}$ right $1$ unit and down $1$ unit. The point of inflection is $(1,-1)$, and the curve is increasing.

For the $y$-intercept, use $x=0$:
$\begin{aligned}y&=(0-1)^{3}-1\\&=-2\end{aligned}$

For the $x$-intercept, the transformed curve reaches $y=0$ when its original height is $1$. On $y=x^{3}$ this occurs at $(1,1)$; shifting gives $(2,0)$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[black,<->] (-1.2,0)--(3.3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,<->] (0,-3.4)--(0,2.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[curveblue,thick,<->,smooth,samples=101,domain=-0.3:2.45,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{(\x-1)*(\x-1)*(\x-1)-1});
\fill[black] (1,-1) circle (1.5pt);
\path (1,-1) node[below right] {$(1,-1)$};
\fill[black] (0,-2) circle (1.5pt);
\path (0,-2) node[left] {$(0,-2)$};
\fill[black] (2,0) circle (1.5pt);
\path (2,0) node[below right] {$(2,0)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

