The graph has the form $y=k(x-b)^{3}+c$. Which equation could represent it?
A. $y=-3(x+1)^{3}+2$
B. $y=3(x+1)^{3}+2$
C. $y=-3(x-1)^{3}+2$
D. $y=-3(x+1)^{3}-2$

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=5mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[black,<->] (-3.2,0)--(1.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,<->] (0,-3)--(0,6.5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[curveblue,thick,<->,smooth,samples=101,domain=-2.1:0.1,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{-3*(\x+1)*(\x+1)*(\x+1)+2});
